### STDOUT
To show a file's content at `HEAD` in Git, you can use the following command:

```sh
git show HEAD:<path-to-file>
```

This command will display the content of the specified file as it exists in the `HEAD` commit.

For example, if you want to see the content of a file named `example.txt`, you would run:

```sh
git show HEAD:example.txt
```

This is useful for checking the current state of a file in your repository.

